Package: michka-kiosk
Version: __VERSION__
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Michka <michka@localhost>
Depends: michka-hub (>= __VERSION__), cage, chromium, libegl1, libgles2, libgl1-mesa-dri, grim, wlr-randr, curl, pipewire, pipewire-pulse, pipewire-alsa, wireplumber, fonts-noto-cjk
Description: Michka kiosk display add-on (cage + Chromium on tty1)
 Turns a machine running the Michka hub into a self-contained touchscreen appliance: a
 wlroots-based Wayland kiosk (cage) launches Chromium full-screen against the local hub on
 tty1 at boot, with no desktop or display manager. Installing this package pulls in the full
 display stack (cage, Chromium, Mesa, grim, wlr-randr, PipeWire for audio) and switches the hub to run as root so
 it can drive the panel (screensaver screen-power, kiosk restart, exit-to-login). Removing it
 reverts the hub to the unprivileged user.
 .
 Designed for small touchscreens (e.g. a 1280x400 mini-rack panel). The screensaver "sleep"
 mode and Chinese font rendering need wlr-randr and fonts-noto-cjk respectively.
